{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0002": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-restrict-basis-equivalence-structures}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-f-map}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-f-map-sets-algebraic-structures}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:73b7a295e0aed410f5378a4b41d05de504bb6f725b2bb9c11fcd70c062cf1d9a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b530be7b131aa7a212f8477541dace3ba236514bc2e45b623d66c6181144520", "source_text": "This is trivial because the collection of maps\namounts to a morphism between the restrictions\nof <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> to <MATH_0003>.\nBy Lemma <REF_0001>\nthis is the same as giving a morphism from <MATH_0004>\nto <MATH_0005>, which by Lemma <REF_0002>\nis the same as an <MATH_0006>-map. See also\nLemma <REF_0003>\nand the discussion preceding it\nfor how to deal with the case of sheaves of algebraic structures.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57a60907aab1db721b40e8e187e9cbfd5ee8a2e72fa906c23f67a82689b2c7c8", "unit_id": "tag:009V:proof"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0735b88cea6d958336921db5f0798d8e6d4c98e15270f97bb396102542b9c955", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the analogue for ringed spaces.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8e836e6a016533002a6b2fd89c3a5432473260d335c9412cc83b920cf53ec23d", "unit_id": "tag:009H:prose-0013"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (X, \\mathcal{O}_X) \\to (Y, \\mathcal{O}_Y)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0007": "$Y$", "MATH_0008": "$V \\in \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y(V)$", "MATH_0010": "$$\n\\varphi_V :\n\\mathcal{G}(V)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V)\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}(f^{-1}V)$", "MATH_0012": "$f^\\sharp_V : \\mathcal{O}_Y(V) \\to \\mathcal{O}_X(f^{-1}V)$", "MATH_0013": "$f$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$\\varphi : \\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\varphi_V$", "MATH_0017": "$V \\in \\mathcal{B}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-ringed-spaces-functoriality-modules}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-f-map-basis-below-modules}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ca0c045b4bea30d3e905739db76eee11c4286bf74101aa0bdc7c3f0f054d2ac4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6870aae3e71d77374df14fbc16feddbd329205686c445a4b9fdff6c905edd4cf", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a morphism of ringed spaces.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a sheaf of <MATH_0005>-modules.\nLet <MATH_0006> be a basis for the topology on <MATH_0007>.\nSuppose given for every <MATH_0008> a\n<MATH_0009>-module map\n<MATH_0010>\n(where <MATH_0011> has a module structure using\n<MATH_0012>)\ncompatible with restriction mappings.\nThen there is a unique <MATH_0013>-map (see discussion of <MATH_0014>-maps in\nSection <REF_0001>)\n<MATH_0015>\nrecovering <MATH_0016> for <MATH_0017>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:88d6193b92042c99c23d0d68b09fdcab198151b6ce06d3a5fb41884dcc2126d6", "unit_id": "tag:009W:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "009H", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fe46702c37eb29d52532b8db8afd86325991aa503a2dc6aa725e49085374b0c9", "source_text": "Same as the proof of the corresponding lemma\nfor sheaves of algebraic structures above.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:554bcc3604f3201ccb3ebf54ee79aa595f72eac020a6986a50b6dbd0a314075c", "unit_id": "tag:009W:proof"}
